The pharmaceutical and biotechnology sectors continue to drive substantial demand for peptones, where they serve as fundamental components in microbial culture media. With biologics production scaling globally, manufacturers increasingly rely on peptones to support cell growth in vaccine development, monoclonal antibody production, and antibiotic manufacturing. The versatility of these nitrogen-rich compounds makes them indispensable for maintaining optimal fermentation conditions.
