What is Peptone?
Peptone represents a category of organic compounds derived through protein hydrolysis, typically sourced from animal tissues (meat, casein, gelatin), plants (soy, wheat), or microbial materials. These complex mixtures of peptides and amino acids serve as indispensable growth factors in microbial and cell culture applications. Their ability to provide essential nitrogen sources while stimulating cellular metabolism makes them particularly valuable in both research and industrial settings.
